# Messages for fraud.scores: one score per order, keyed by order id.
#
# Small records with a flat shape and a number in them that means something. This is the topic to
# open when you want to try a message filter and see it match a handful of records out of a few:
# "score above 0.8" is three of these, and they are the three an analyst would actually want.
#
# It is also read by a LIVE consumer group in the demo — `fraud-scoring`, which restarts one of
# its two members on a timer so the group passes through a real rebalance every minute or so. That
# is the only way to see a rebalancing group at all: a healthy group rebalances once when it
# starts and then never again.
#
# The keys are order ids that exist in orders.v1, so a score can be followed back to the order it
# is about, and one order (ORD-10251) is scored twice because the model was re-run after the
# payment was declined.
#mode: key-value

ORD-10241\t{"orderId":"ORD-10241","scoredAt":"%TS-5390%","score":0.04,"decision":"ALLOW","model":"fraud-v7","features":{"customerAgeDays":812,"ordersLast24h":1,"billingShippingMatch":true,"newDevice":false}}
